OpenClaw v2026.8.1: retire managed npm plugins without following Windows junctions.

Base: ea806575e6450e4d1efdfc72c19f04be982a1b9b.

Electron 43.5.0 / embedded Node 24.19.0 traverses a nested junction during
fs.rmSync({ recursive: true }); plain Node 24.19.0 does not. The managed npm
plugin peer link points at the bundled host runtime, so doctor cleanup can
delete dist workers and prevent every subsequent gateway startup.

Stage the entire retirement batch outside node_modules before changing npm
metadata. Preserve original package/lock bytes, roll back failed publication,
and clean committed payloads with explicit lstat/unlink/non-recursive rmdir.
Locked cleanup debris stays in a reported quarantine; failed rollback retains
recovery files and still blocks. The captured install-record baseline and
public doctor call remain unchanged. No global fs patch or plugin-id special case.

